Z||000000||WGraffiKs||01-12-2000||03:45 PM||||In my 86.5 GT, the gas gauge has always been a bit off.  When the tank is very nearly empty, the gauge still shows slightly above the last "E" mark.  Also is pegged fully right when tank is full.  Is there any way to adjust it to align it when empty (much more important to me than when she's full!  At least the system was made so that when I hit the brakes when the tank is nearly empty, the small amount of gas left shows as a "jump" in the gauge! That tells me there's enough left to limp into a station!  Is the sending unit inside the tank?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||01-12-2000||04:52 PM||||No GM gas gage is accurate. There is something about this in your manual, I think.||||reg||1
